# Only the generated page and its logos belong on a public deployment.
#
# Everything else here is pipeline input or intermediate data, and one item is
# a licence problem rather than merely noise: buyme-chains-google.json is raw
# Google Places output. The repository git-ignores it because Places forbids
# retaining those coordinates, and serving it as a downloadable file is bulk
# redistribution of that data — worse than the page, which merely displays it.
# The OSM-derived JSON raises the same share-alike question in miniature.
#
# Deployed: buyme-map-google.html, logos/, logos-tav/ and logos-swish/.
*.json
*.mjs
*.md
buyme-data.js
buyme-map-osm.html
google-page-template.html
.cache/
lib/
